# Generated by tools/spheres_traditions.py from pinned Ultimate rules.
# Sphere-specific drawbacks grant a bonus talent in their own sphere.
Sphere Drawback - Beast Soul	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Alteration Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Alteration Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:You cannot bestow the Blank Transformation, including through the Anthropomorphic Transformation talent. You must select a [transformation] talent with the bonus talent gained from this drawback. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc71
Sphere Drawback - Fleshwarper	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Alteration Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Alteration Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Lycanthropic	DESC:You may not target yourself with shapeshift. Incompatible: Lycanthropic Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc72
Sphere Drawback - Lycanthropic	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Alteration Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Alteration Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Fleshwarper	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Rebound	DESC:You can only target yourself with your shapeshift ability. You cannot gain the Mass Alteration nor Ranged Alteration talents. Incompatible: Fleshwarper, Rebound Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc73
Sphere Drawback - Rebound	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Alteration Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Alteration Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Lycanthropic	DESC:If an unwilling creature succeeds on a save to resist your shapeshift effect, you must save against the same effect at the same DC. On a failed save, you receive all the traits and forms you would have granted the target. This effect lasts for 1d4 rounds. You must select Animal Mind or Twisted Shapeshift with the bonus talent gained from this drawback. Incompatible: Lycanthropic Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc74
Sphere Drawback - Shapesnatcher	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Alteration Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Alteration Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Source: Expanded Spheres: Baron's Lost Apocrypha Your forms require an initial inspiration which you draw from. You gain the Steal Shape talent as your bonus talent for this drawback, but you can only use your shapeshift when Steal Shape is triggered. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc75
Sphere Drawback - Transformative Brew	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Alteration Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Alteration Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:You must select the Instill Shapeshift talent with the bonus talent granted by this drawback, and you can only use your Alteration sphere abilities through this talent. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc76
Sphere Drawback - Unnatural Transformation	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Alteration Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Alteration Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Creatures under the effect of your shapeshift bear irrepressible signs [coloration, visual aura, glowing sigil or similar] of their true identity. Your shapeshift never grants a bonus to Disguise checks due to the obviously unnatural nature of the transformation. When touched by silver [such as being hit with a silver weapon or even touched by a silver piece] a creature under the effect of your shapeshift must attempt a Will save with a DC equal 5 + any damage dealt or have the shapeshift end immediately. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc77
Sphere Drawback - Cruoromancy	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Blood Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Blood Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Hemokinetic	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Limited Acceleration	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Self-Controlled	DESC:You cannot use blood control. You must select any [blood art] talent with the bonus talent from this drawback. Incompatible: Hemokinetic, Limited Acceleration, Self-Controlled. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc79
Sphere Drawback - Hemokinetic	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Blood Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Blood Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Limited Acceleration	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Self-Controlled	DESC:You cannot use blood control. You must select the Hemokinesis talent with the bonus talent from this drawback. You may use the blood arc option on creatures within blood control range [and may take the Improved Range talent] even when they are not under your blood control. You may use the Hemokinesis options dependant on the Manipulate Alchemy and Manipulate Health talents, but only when the necessary ability has been used by another creature. Incompatible: Limited Acceleration, Self-controlled Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc80
Sphere Drawback - Humors	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Blood Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Blood Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:You must select the Instill Blood Control talent with the bonus talent granted by this drawback, and you can only use your Blood sphere abilities through this talent. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc81
Sphere Drawback - Limited Acceleration	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Blood Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Blood Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Hemokinetic	DESC:Choose either [quicken] or [still]. You can only use this ability and cannot use abilities of the other type. Incompatible: Hemokinetic Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc82
Sphere Drawback - Self-Controlled	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Blood Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Blood Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Hemokinetic	DESC:You may only target yourself with blood control. You must select the Self Control talent with the bonus talent from this drawback. Incompatible: Hemokinetic Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc83
Sphere Drawback - Caller	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Conjuration Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Conjuration Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:You do not gain the summon ability of the Conjuration sphere. You must select the Call Planar Creature advanced talent with the bonus talent gained from this drawback. This drawback may not be selected if the Call Planar Creature advanced talent is not permitted in your campaign. Incompatible: Any Conjuration drawback that affects the summon ability or companions granted by it. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc85
Sphere Drawback - Constant Link	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Conjuration Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Conjuration Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Maintaining your companion’s presence requires concentration. You may not spend a spell point to continue the duration of summon without concentration nor take any talents that would allow you to maintain the summon without concentration. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc86
Sphere Drawback - Divided Soul	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Conjuration Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Conjuration Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Your Conjuration sphere companions share a single pool of Hit Dice. The Hit Dice of all your companions combined is equal to your caster level [with a minimum of 1 Hit Die per companion]. When you gain a caster level, you may choose which companion gains the additional Hit Die, but no single companion can have Hit Dice exceeding 2/3 your caster level. If this calculation would result in companions with less than 1 Hit Die, such a companion instead has 1 Hit Die, but has their hit points reduced by half and takes a -1 penalty on all d20 rolls. Calculate the companion’s Hit Dice prior to applying the effects of any companion template. You must take Extra Companion with the bonus talent gained from this drawback. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc87
Sphere Drawback - Elongated Summoning	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Conjuration Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Conjuration Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Summoning a creature requires 1 minute of concentrated effort, rather than only a standard action. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc88
Sphere Drawback - Figment Companion	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Conjuration Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Conjuration Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Your companions are only semi-real projections. The first time each round a creature is affected by an effect originating from your companions, such as attacks or sphere effects, it may attempt a Will save versus your Conjuration sphere DC to negate the effect and any others originating from your companion before the start of the creature’s next turn. Succeeding on this save grants a +2 bonus on future saves made against that same companion for the next 24 hours. [As usual, this bonus does not stack with itself.] Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc89
Sphere Drawback - Life Merger	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Conjuration Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Conjuration Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Your companions are tied directly to your own life force. Whenever one of your Conjuration companions would take damage, you suffer an equal amount of damage. This damage cannot be reduced or redirected. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc90
Sphere Drawback - Limited Range	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Conjuration Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Conjuration Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Source: Spheres Apocrypha: Cohorts & Companions Your companions must remain at a close proximity with you or lose effectiveness. Your companions must remain within 5 feet + 5 feet per 5 points of magic skill bonus you possess, and cannot move beyond this distance without being dismissed. If your moving would cause your companion to be beyond this range, your companion may take a movement action outside of their turn [which provokes attacks of opportunity as normal] to try to end up back in the area. If successful the companion is not dismissed and is staggered on their next turn. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc91
Sphere Drawback - Material Weakness	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Conjuration Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Conjuration Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Choose cold iron, silver, or wood [or another special material with GM’s explicit approval]. When touched by an object primarily composed of the chosen material, your companion must attempt a Will save with a DC equal to 10 + any damage dealt by the object or be dismissed from the plane. The companion may not be summoned again for 1 hour. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc92
Sphere Drawback - Object Bound	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Conjuration Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Conjuration Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Choose an object you possess for each companion you gain [for example: a small oil lamp, a ring, or a sword]. Such objects count as magic items of the Conjuration sphere using your caster level for the item’s caster level, though you may still enchant them with other effects normally. If enchanted separately, the other effects on the item may be suppressed using dispel effects separately from the magic property granted by this drawback, using the caster level of those enchantments for determining the MSD of those effects. You must drop or throw this object as part of summoning the companion. This does not affect the casting time, though additional actions may be required to draw the object. If this object is broken or destroyed, you cannot summon the corresponding companion. While the companion is present, the object is visible on the companion and may be targeted with the sunder maneuver, dispel effects, and other effects that can target attended magical items. While part of the companion, the object emits a sign that draws attention to itself, usually glowing. If the object is broken, destroyed, or has its magic suppressed, the companion immediately disappears and may not be summoned again until the object is repaired or replaced. Attuning a new object requires a 24 hour ritual. Any damage dealt to the object is also dealt to the companion without being further affected by damage reduction, immunity, resistance, or vulnerability. You may choose to have a single item for any or all of your companions, but no more than one companion can be summoned at a time using a single item. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc93
Sphere Drawback - Counterfeit	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Creation Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Creation Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Limited Creation	DESC:When you create an object, it must be of the same shape, size, and material of another object you can perceive. You must select Exquisite Detail with this drawback. Incompatible: Limited Creation [alter] Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc95
Sphere Drawback - Down To Earth	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Creation Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Creation Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Limited Creation	DESC:Source: Spheres Apocrypha: Casting Traditions Your objects are all rooted to a surface and you cannot create objects in mid-air. All your creations must be created on a surface large enough to hold them. You gain the Created Momentum talent as the bonus talent from this drawback and may still create objects with momentum, but this does not allow the object to detach itself from a surface in the process of creation [meaning you can only target creatures that are on the surface where the created object is going to be]. Incompatible: Limited Creation [alter] Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc96
Sphere Drawback - Fission	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Creation Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Creation Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Limited Creation	DESC:When creating objects, you do so by splitting off part of your body: this inflicts 1d4 points of damage + 1d4 per size category of the object or objects above Small to be created. This damage bypasses temporary hit points, and cannot be healed as long as the object or objects exist. However, you may reabsorb the created object by touching it as a free action, causing you to heal damage equal to that expended to create it. If an object has the broken condition when it is reabsorbed you only gain 1/2 the hit points back. If the object is destroyed you cannot reabsorb it but may heal normally. You may dismiss any object created in this way regardless of distance. Doing so does not restore the lost hit points but allows you to recover normally as if the object was destroyed. Even through Distant Creation or other options, you cannot create objects further away from you than adjacent spaces. You must take either the Created Momentum, Exquisite Detail, or Practiced Creation talent with the bonus talent gained from this drawback. Incompatible: Limited Creation [alter] Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc97
Sphere Drawback - Limited Creation	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Creation Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Creation Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Choose either alter or create. You can only use this ability. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc98
Sphere Drawback - Material Focus	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Creation Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Creation Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Water Wizard	DESC:You may only create or alter objects of a single, special substance such as wood, stone, bones, gas, etc. If the material in question would require a [material] talent to use, you must choose that [material] talent as the talent gained from this drawback. You cannot gain any other [material] talent. If you choose a material not available from 1st caster level [for example: iron or gold], this does not allow you to create or alter that material before your caster level is high enough. Incompatible: Water Wizard Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc99
Sphere Drawback - Material Mimic	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Creation Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Creation Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:In order to create or alter objects you must be in physical contact with another object that is composed of the material that will result from the effect and no more than three size categories smaller [e.g. to create a Medium iron object, you would need to be touching another iron object of Diminutive size or larger]. If you possess Change Material then this restricts the materials you can change the targeted object into. You may not use your own body as a blueprint, but you may use other creatures, if applicable. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc100
Sphere Drawback - Water Wizard	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Creation Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Creation Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Material Focus	DESC:You may only create or alter water, ice, and steam. You lose the ability to create or alter vegetable matter and instead can create or alter water in its solid, liquid, or gaseous forms. You gain Gaseous Generation as the bonus talent gained from this drawback, but can only use it to affect steam. You cannot gain any other [material] talents. Incompatible: Material Focus Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc101
Sphere Drawback - Black Spot	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Dark Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Dark Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Meld Into Dark	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Penumbra	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Shadow Master	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Shadowed Brew	DESC:Your area of darkness is only a 5-foot radius, and cannot be increased in any way. You cannot select talents that change the area of your darkness [such as Greater Darkness, Shifting Shadows, or Wall Of Darkness]. You must select a [darkness] talent as your bonus talent for this drawback. Incompatible: Meld Into Dark, Penumbra, Shadow Master, Shadowed Brew Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc103
Sphere Drawback - Cloaking Darkness	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Dark Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Dark Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Meld Into Dark	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Penumbra	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Shadow Master	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Shadowed Brew	DESC:You are adept at turning a target’s own shadow against them, but your ability to craft areas of darkness from nothing is lacking. You must select Ranged Darkness as the bonus talent gained from this drawback. You may use [shadow] talents at this increased range, but you cannot form and maintain areas of darkness or blot unless you are standing within their area of effect. Incompatible: Meld Into Dark, Penumbra, Shadow Master, Shadowed Brew Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc104
Sphere Drawback - Crepuscular	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Dark Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Dark Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Your magic draws on the interplay of darkness and light and the contrast of shadows rather than pure blackness. You may not use Dark sphere talents when you are positioned within lighting conditions of darkness or bright light, even if they were created by your own magic. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc105
Sphere Drawback - Meld Into Dark	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Dark Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Dark Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Black Spot	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Cloaking Darkness	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Penumbra	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Shadow Dependance	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Shadow Master	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Shadowed Brew	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Subtle Shade	DESC:You cannot create darkness, and cannot select [darkness] talents. You gain the Greater Meld talent as the bonus talent gained by this drawback. Incompatible: Black Spot, Cloaking Darkness, Penumbra, Shadow Dependance, Shadow Master, Shadowed Brew, Subtle Shade Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc106
Sphere Drawback - Penumbra	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Dark Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Dark Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Black Spot	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Cloaking Darkness	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Meld Into Dark	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Shadow Dependance	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Shadow Master	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Shadowed Brew	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Subtle Shade	DESC:You cannot create darkness, and cannot select [darkness] talents. You must select the Dampen Light talent as your bonus talent for this drawback. Incompatible: Black Spot, Cloaking Darkness, Meld Into Dark, Shadow Dependance, Shadow Master, Shadowed Brew, Subtle Shade Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc107
Sphere Drawback - Personal Meld	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Dark Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Dark Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:You cannot grant a meld to another creature; you can only use them on yourself. You must select Quick Meld with the bonus talent gained by this drawback. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc108
Sphere Drawback - Shadow Aura	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Dark Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Dark Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Cloaking Darkness	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Meld Into Dark	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Penumbra	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Shadow Master	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Shadowed Brew	DESC:You must select Clinging Darkness with this drawback. When you create darkness, you must target yourself such that the darkness clings to you. Incompatible: Cloaking Darkness, Meld Into Dark, Penumbra, Shadow Master, Shadowed Brew Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc109
Sphere Drawback - Shadow Dependance	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Dark Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Dark Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Meld Into Dark	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Penumbra	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Shadow Master	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Shadowed Brew	DESC:Rather than summon darkness from nothing, you draw upon your own shadow to produce your magic. You stretch and manipulate your shadow to create areas of darkness or blot, and may only have one active at any given time. When your darkness or blot is active you do not cast a shadow and cannot use or be the target of abilities or talents that depend on possessing a shadow. You may otherwise use [shadow] and [meld] talents normally. Incompatible: Meld Into Dark, Penumbra, Shadow Master, Shadowed Brew Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc110
Sphere Drawback - Shadow Master	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Dark Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Dark Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Black Spot	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Cloaking Darkness	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Meld Into Dark	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Penumbra	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Shadow Dependance	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Subtle Shade	DESC:You cannot create darkness, and cannot select [darkness] talents. You must select a [shadow] talent as your bonus talent for this drawback. Incompatible: Black Spot, Cloaking Darkness, Meld Into Dark, Penumbra, Shadow Dependance, Subtle Shade Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc111
Sphere Drawback - Shadowed Brew	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Dark Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Dark Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Black Spot	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Cloaking Darkness	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Crepuscular	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Penumbra	DESC:You must select the Instill Dark talent with the bonus talent granted by this drawback, and you can only use your Dark sphere abilities through this talent. You must possess either the Meld Into Dark or Shadow Master drawback to select this drawback. Incompatible: Black Spot, Cloaking Darkness, Crepuscular, Penumbra, Shadow Dependence. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc112
Sphere Drawback - Subtle Shade	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Dark Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Dark Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Meld Into Dark	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Penumbra	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Shadow Master	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Shadowed Brew	DESC:You must select the Insinuate talent with the bonus talent granted by this drawback. You cannot create darkness except for blots, and must use the Insinuate talent when creating blots. Incompatible: Meld Into Dark, Penumbra, Shadow Master, Shadowed Brew. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc113
Sphere Drawback - Death To The Living	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Death Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Death Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Flesh Artisan	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Necromantic Limit	DESC:The only actions undead you reanimate understand are “attack”, “fall” [causing them to fall prone as a free action], and “rise” [causing them to stand up from prone]. While prone, they will still attack creatures within reach and will spend their move action to move 5 feet, but will not rise until commanded. If you do not direct your undead to attack a creature each round, they act as though confused [you are considered part of their “self”, but other allies are not]. You may not select talents that increase your ability to communicate with your undead, such as Undead Whisperer or Master’s Presence. You must select Reanimated Warriors as the bonus talent gained through this drawback. Incompatible: Flesh Artisan, Necromantic Limit [ghost strike] Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc115
Sphere Drawback - Deathful Touch	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Death Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Death Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Flesh Artisan	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Necromantic Concoction	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Necromantic Limit	DESC:You may only use ghost strike as a melee touch attack. If you use the Cryptic Strike talent, you can only do so with melee attacks. You must take a talent that augments ghost strike with the drawback. Incompatible: Flesh Artisan, Necromantic Concoction, Necromantic Limit [reanimate], Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc116
Sphere Drawback - Favored Undead	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Death Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Death Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Flesh Artisan	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Necromantic Limit	DESC:You gain the Expanded Necromancy talent with the bonus talent gained by this drawback. Choose one variant undead [such as bloody skeleton, burning skeleton, fast zombie, or plague zombie]. Whenever you reanimate a creature, you must use this talent and may only reanimate creatures as the chosen variant. Incompatible: Flesh Artisan, Necromantic Limit [ghost strike] Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc117
Sphere Drawback - Flesh Artisan	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Death Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Death Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Death To The Living	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Deathful Touch	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Favored Undead	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Necromantic Limit	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Necromantic Concoction	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Undead Trainer	DESC:You do not gain ghost strike nor reanimate. You gain both Corpse Manipulation and Tomb Of Flesh with the bonus talents granted by this drawback. This drawback counts as two drawbacks, and ghost strike and reanimate must be bought back separately. Incompatible: Death To The Living, Deathful Touch, Favored Undead, Necromantic Limit, Necromantic Concoction, Undead Trainer Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc118
Sphere Drawback - Necromantic Concoction	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Death Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Death Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Deathful Touch	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Flesh Artisan	DESC:You must select the Instill Death talent with the bonus talent granted by this drawback, and you can only use your Death sphere abilities through this talent. Incompatible: Deathful Touch, Flesh Artisan Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc119
Sphere Drawback - Necromantic Limit	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Death Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Death Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Flesh Artisan	DESC:Choose either ghost strike or reanimate. You can only use this ability and cannot use the one not chosen. Incompatible: Flesh Artisan Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc120
Sphere Drawback - Spiritual Voyager	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Death Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Death Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Death To The Living	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Deathful Touch	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Favored Undead	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Flesh Artisan	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Necromantic Limit	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Necromantic Concoction	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Undead Trainer	DESC:You do not gain ghost strike nor reanimate. You gain both Astral Projection and Project Spirit with the bonus talents granted by this drawback. This drawback counts as two drawbacks, and the ghost strike and reanimate abilities must be bought back separately. If a character does not initially meet the prerequisites for Astral Projection or Project Spirit when they gain this talent, they do not gain the benefits of either talent until they meet the prerequisites for them. Incompatible: Death To The Living, Deathful Touch, Favored Undead, Flesh Artisan, Necromantic Limit, Necromantic Concoction, Undead Trainer Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc121
Sphere Drawback - Undead Trainer	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Death Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Death Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Flesh Artisan	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Necromantic Limit	DESC:Choose a creature type [other than undead] from the ranger favored enemies table. You may only reanimate dead creatures of the chosen type [and subtype, if applicable]. For every 5 caster levels you possess, you may choose an additional creature type. You may choose ‘construct’ for a creature type, in which case it allows you to reanimate necrotic marionettes. You must select Undead Whisperer with the bonus talent gained through this drawback. Incompatible: Flesh Artisan, Necromantic Limit [ghost strike] Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc122
Sphere Drawback - Aligned Combatant	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Destruction Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Destruction Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Choose an end of the alignment spectrum that you possess [good, evil, lawful, or chaotic]. Your destructive blast deals no damage to creatures who possess this alignment and full damage to creatures of the opposite alignment [evil for good, lawful for chaotic, etc.]. Neutral creatures [those who possess neither your selected alignment nor its opposite] suffer only half damage from your destructive blast. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc124
Sphere Drawback - Destructive Touch	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Destruction Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Destruction Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Shape Focus	DESC:Your destructive blast’s range decreases from close to touch; you cannot use it to make ranged attacks. While you may still apply [blast shape] talents to your destructive blast, they cannot extend further than your natural reach [or the reach of your melee weapon, if using Energy Strike; you cannot use Energy Strike to make ranged attacks]. Incompatible: Shape Focus Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc125
Sphere Drawback - Energy Focus	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Destruction Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Destruction Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Choose a blast type group. You may only make destructive blasts from that blast type group. You must select a [blast type] talent from the chosen blast type group with the bonus talent granted by this drawback. You may not select any other [blast type] talents outside the chosen blast type group. Author's Note: A blast type talent that is in multiple blast type groups counts as being outside your chosen blast type group and cannot be selected, even if one of the groups would match your chosen blast type group. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc126
Sphere Drawback - Shape Focus	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Destruction Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Destruction Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Destructive Touch	DESC:You may only make a destructive blast of a single shape. You must select a [blast shape] talent with the bonus talented granted by this drawback, and cannot make destructive blasts except when using that [blast shape]. You may not select any other [blast shape] talents. Incompatible: Destructive Touch Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc127
Sphere Drawback - Soft Blaster	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Destruction Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Destruction Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Source: Expanded Spheres: Baron's Lost Apocrypha You gain the Damage Control talent as a bonus talent. Whenever you make a destructive blast, you must always choose to deal no damage with your blast. You gain an additional Destruction talent in addition to Damage Control when you take this drawback. If you buy off this Drawback, you lose Damage Control as a bonus talent. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc128
Sphere Drawback - Uncontrolled Blaster	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Destruction Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Destruction Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Energy Focus	DESC:You gain the Erratic Blast [blast type] talent. You can only use the Erratic Blast [blast type] talent. Note that this drawback uses an advanced talent and should be used at GM discretion. Incompatible: Energy Focus Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc129
Sphere Drawback - Divining Concoction	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Divination Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Divination Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:You must select the Instill Divination talent with the bonus talent granted by this drawback, and you can only use your Divination sphere abilities through this talent. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc131
Sphere Drawback - Limited Divination	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Divination Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Divination Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Choose either sense or divine. You can only use this ability and cannot use the other type. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc132
Sphere Drawback - Limited Penetration	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Divination Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Divination Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Limited Divination	DESC:When using Divination talents or abilities to divine you cannot penetrate solid objects. You must select a [divine] talent with the bonus talent granted by this drawback. Incompatible: Limited Divination [sense] Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc133
Sphere Drawback - Hidden Magic	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Divination Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Divination Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:You do not gain the base divine ability to detect magic, nor the base sense ability to decipher magical text. You may still gain other senses through magic talents and gain the ability to detect other things [undead, charms, etc.] through the divine ability. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc134
Sphere Drawback - Shaped Divination	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Divination Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Divination Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Limited Divination	DESC:Your divine area changes to a cone rather than a sphere centered upon yourself. You may take this drawback a second time, limiting your ability to only divine targets inside a line instead of a cone. This drawback does in no other way change the range at which you may divine targets. In regards to this drawback, your divination shape [be it cone or line] remains fixed pointing in one direction, and once each round as a free action you may change the direction of the shape. You must select [divine] talent[s] with the bonus talent[s] granted by this drawback. Incompatible: Limited Divination [sense] Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc135
Sphere Drawback - Bodily Enhancement	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Enhancement Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Enhancement Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Constructor	DESC:You cannot enhance equipment and objects, only creatures. You can only take talents which can affect creatures. You must choose an [enhance] talent or Natural Enhancement with the bonus talent gained by this drawback. Incompatible: Constructor Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc137
Sphere Drawback - Constructor	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Enhancement Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Enhancement Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Bodily Enhancement	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Personal Magics	DESC:You cannot use any effect of the Enhancement sphere that does not create a creature or mind. You must use the bonus magic talent from this drawback to select either Animate Object or Bestow Intelligence. Incompatible: Bodily Enhancement, Personal Magics Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc138
Sphere Drawback - Marking Enhancements	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Enhancement Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Enhancement Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:A mark appears on any creature or object you enhance. This mark always appears on a body part or portion of the object where it is easily visible. The mark can be easily removed; it can be rubbed away as a standard action [which requires a touch attack and provokes an attack of opportunity if the creature is not willing], or fades away after being exposed to water or another solvent for one minute. Once the mark has been removed, the enhancement ends prematurely. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc139
Sphere Drawback - Personal Magics	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Enhancement Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Enhancement Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Constructor	DESC:You may only enhance yourself and your own equipment. You cannot take the Ranged Enhancement talent, and any enhancement bestowed on an object ceases to function unless you are carrying, wearing, or wielding that object. You cannot take talents such as Bestow Intelligence or Animate Object that give life or minds to objects. Incompatible: Constructor Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc140
Sphere Drawback - Power Leech	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Enhancement Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Enhancement Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:You must select Power Parasitism with this talent. You can only use your Enhancement sphere abilities when Power Parasitism is triggered. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc141
Sphere Drawback - Special Delivery	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Enhancement Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Enhancement Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:You must choose the Instill Enhancement talent with the bonus talent gained from this drawback. You cannot create enhancements except by using Instill Enhancement. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc142
Sphere Drawback - Terrain-Bonded	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Fallen Fey Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Fallen Fey Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Choose one terrain. Your fey-link only works while you are in that terrain. If a creature with your fey-link leaves your chosen terrain, your fey-link, and any ongoing fey-blessings, are suppressed until they reenter your chosen terrain. Consult the ranger list of favored terrains to see potential terrain types. You may change your chosen terrain by spending one week continuously in the same terrain. You must choose Fey Secrets, Listen To The Wind, or Wild Walker with the bonus talent gained by this drawback. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc144
Sphere Drawback - Cursed Brew	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Fate Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Fate Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:You must select the Instill Fate talent with the bonus talent granted by this drawback, and you can only use your Fate sphere abilities through this talent. You must possess the Tongue Of Ages drawback to gain this one. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc146
Sphere Drawback - Luckless	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Fate Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Fate Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Tongue Of Ages	DESC:You cannot use the Serendipity consecration. You must choose a [consecration] talent with the bonus talent gained from this drawback. Incompatible: Tongue Of Ages Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc147
Sphere Drawback - Neutrality	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Fate Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Fate Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Sanctified	DESC:You lack a strong connection to any alignment type. You cannot use the Hallow word. You must choose a [word] talent with the bonus talent gained from this drawback. Incompatible: Sanctified Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc148
Sphere Drawback - Non-Judgemental	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Fate Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Fate Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Your Fate sphere abilities treat creatures as not possessing an alignment unless they possess the chaotic, evil, good, or lawful subtypes or draw their abilities from a source with such subtypes [gods should generally be considered outsiders with subtypes corresponding to their alignment for the purposes of this drawback]. Such creatures are treated as if they had alignments corresponding to their subtypes. You must use this drawback to select one of the following talents: Align Object, Divine Force, Divine Pressure, or Enmity. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc149
Sphere Drawback - Personal Fate	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Fate Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Fate Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:You may only target yourself with your words and motifs, and your consecrations only affect you. You cannot take Echoing Word or any other talent that would increase the range or expand the targets for your Fate sphere effects. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc150
Sphere Drawback - Sanctified	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Fate Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Fate Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Neutrality	DESC:You may not create words. Incompatible: Neutrality Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc151
Sphere Drawback - Tongue Of Ages	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Fate Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Fate Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Luckless	DESC:You may not create consecrations. Incompatible: Luckless Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc152
Sphere Drawback - Disappearance	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Illusion Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Illusion Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Theme Fixation	DESC:You cannot create illusions or tricks, except to make suppressions. You must select the Suppression talent as your bonus talent for this drawback. Incompatible: Theme Fixation Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc154
Sphere Drawback - Glamered Brew	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Illusion Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Illusion Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Personal Illusion	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Theme Fixation	DESC:You must select the Instill Glamer talent with the bonus talent granted by this drawback, and you can only use your Illusion sphere abilities through this talent. You must possess the Obscura Mage drawback to select this one. Incompatible: Personal Illusion, Theme Fixation Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc155
Sphere Drawback - Limited Sensation	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Illusion Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Illusion Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:You may not take additional [sensory] talents from the Illusion sphere. Your illusions lose the sight descriptor granted by the base Illusion sphere. You must take a [sensory] talent as the bonus talent granted by this drawback. If you select Illusionary Touch as the bonus talent granted by this drawback you are not prohibited from taking it a second time. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc156
Sphere Drawback - Obscura Mage	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Illusion Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Illusion Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:You may not create figments with your tricks and illusions. You must select a [glamer] talent as your bonus talent for this drawback, unless you possess the Disappearance drawback in which case you must select a [sensory] talent. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc157
Sphere Drawback - Personal Illusion	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Illusion Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Illusion Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Glamered Brew	DESC:Your illusions are directly connected to your body. You can only apply glamers to yourself, and the range of your figments and tricks that target an area is reduced to 0 feet; you may only target squares that you currently occupy and must spend an immediate action any time your location changes to direct all figments and tricks you are currently maintaining to move with you. To use tricks that target unwilling creatures or objects you must first make a successful melee touch attack. The duration of tricks targeting creatures or objects immediately ends the round you are no longer maintaining physical contact with the target. Incompatible: Glamered Brew Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc158
Sphere Drawback - Theme Fixation	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Illusion Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Illusion Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Disappearance	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Glamered Brew	DESC:You may only create figments and glamers within a specific and narrow theme such as dragons, cubes, insects, cards, weapons, hands, etc. The exact nature of this concept should be worked out with the GM, but as a rule of thumb, this should consist of a consistent singular theme; you might only be able to create figments or glamers of dragons, or be able to create a figment of fire if it originated from the mouth of a dragon glamer. The GM is the final arbiter on whether an image or idea fits into the dedicated theme. You must take a [sensory] talent as the bonus talent granted by this drawback. Incompatible: Disappearance, Glamered Brew Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc159
Sphere Drawback - Tricksters Grudge	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Illusion Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Illusion Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Your illusions only work on one specific type of creature. When you select this drawback you must select a creature type. If you select humanoid or outsider you must also select a subtype. All other creature types automatically disbelieve your illusions and any non-shadow effects that would persist even if disbelieved have no effect on them. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc160
Sphere Drawback - Fueled by Futility	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Life Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Life Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Glorious	DESC:You must select Violent Recuperation with this talent. You can only use your Life abilities when Violent Recuperation is triggered. Incompatible: Glorious Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc162
Sphere Drawback - Glorious	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Life Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Life Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Medicinal	DESC:You are not a healer, you are a soldier, and life cannot be given before it is taken. You cannot use your Life sphere abilities without successfully attacking a worthy enemy first. You gain the Taste Of Victory talent as your bonus talent for this drawback, but you can only use your Life abilities when Taste Of Victory is triggered. Incompatible: Medicinal Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc163
Sphere Drawback - Inhuman Healing	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Life Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Life Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Your cure effects cannot heal living creatures. You gain Esoteric Healing with the bonus talent gained through this drawback. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc164
Sphere Drawback - Limited Restoration	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Life Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Life Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Choose either restore or cure/invigorate. You can only use this ability or abilities and lose the ability to use the ones not chosen. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc165
Sphere Drawback - Medicinal	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Life Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Life Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Glorious	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Sympathetic	DESC:You must select the Instill Life talent with the bonus talent granted by this drawback, and you can only use your Life sphere abilities through this talent. Incompatible: Glorious, Sympathetic Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc166
Sphere Drawback - Regenerate	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Life Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Life Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Sympathetic	DESC:You may only target yourself with your Life sphere abilities. Incompatible: Sympathetic Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc167
Sphere Drawback - Slow Recovery	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Life Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Life Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Limited Restoration	DESC:You lack the ability to cause rapid healing. You must select the Revitalize talent with the bonus talent granted by this drawback, and cannot use cure unless you use it through the Revitalize talent. Incompatible: Limited Restoration [restore] Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc168
Sphere Drawback - Sympathetic	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Life Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Life Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Limited Restoration	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Medicinal	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Regenerate	DESC:You may only restore others by taking their afflictions unto yourself. You must select the Empathic Healing talent with the bonus talent gained from this drawback and can only use the restore ability with the Empathic Healing talent. Incompatible: Limited Restoration [cure/invigorate], Medicinal, Regenerate Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc169
Sphere Drawback - Unnatural Remedy	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Life Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Life Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Your healing magic may be cold, eerie, harsh, or pervasive. Whenever you use cure, restore, or invigorate on a target [even yourself], they reflexively resist [even while unconscious], and must attempt a Will saving throw against the effect as if they were an unwilling target. On a success, restore is negated and any healing or temporary hit points bestowed by cure or invigorate are halved. Targets cannot choose to fail this saving throw. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc170
Sphere Drawback - Flexible Lens	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Light Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Light Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Light Focus	DESC:You cannot create a Telescope lens. You must choose a [lens] talent with the bonus talent gained from this drawback. Incompatible: Light Focus Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc172
Sphere Drawback - Glowing Brew	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Light Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Light Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Nimbus Focus	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Roving Glow	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Touch Of Light	DESC:You must select the Instill Glow talent with the bonus talent granted by this drawback, and you can only use your Light sphere abilities through this talent. Incompatible: Nimbus Focus, Roving Glow, Touch Of Light Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc173
Sphere Drawback - Lens Focus	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Light Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Light Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Light Focus	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Nimbus Focus	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Roving Glow	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Subtle Light	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Touch Of Light	DESC:You cannot create glow effects. Incompatible: Light Focus, Nimbus Focus, Roving Glow, Subtle Light, Touch Of Light Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc174
Sphere Drawback - Light Focus	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Light Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Light Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Flexible Lens	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Lens Focus	DESC:You cannot create lenses. Incompatible: Flexible Lens, Lens Focus Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc175
Sphere Drawback - Nimbus Focus	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Light Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Light Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Glowing Brew	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Lens Focus	DESC:You may only cause your glows to shed light in a specific shape. You must select a [nimbus] talent with the bonus talent granted by this drawback, and must always apply that [nimbus] talent to your glows. You may not select any other [nimbus] talents. Incompatible: Glowing Brew, Lens Focus Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc176
Sphere Drawback - Roving Glow	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Light Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Light Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Glowing Brew	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Lens Focus	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Touch Of Light	DESC:You cannot place glow effects on objects or creatures. You must select the Dancing Lights talent with the bonus talent gained from this drawback. Incompatible: Glowing Brew, Lens Focus, Touch Of Light Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc177
Sphere Drawback - Subtle Light	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Light Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Light Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Lens Focus	DESC:You must select the Black Light talent as the bonus talent gained from this drawback, and must use this talent on every glow you create. Incompatible: Lens Focus Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc178
Sphere Drawback - Touch Of Light	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Light Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Light Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Glowing Brew	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Lens Focus	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Roving Glow	DESC:You cannot cause objects or creatures to glow as a ranged touch attack, nor create lenses at a range greater than touch. You cannot take Ranged Light, and you may only apply Solar Strike to melee attacks. Incompatible: Glowing Brew, Lens Focus, Roving Glow Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc179
Sphere Drawback - Conservationist	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Mana Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Mana Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:You prize the value of mana, and hate to see it disappear. You cannot use the Spellburn option of the expunge ability. You may not utilize any ability from a talent that deals spell point damage. Abilities that transfer them [such as Manathief] are still able to be used. You must select an [expunge] talent when taking this drawback. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc181
Sphere Drawback - Incongruent	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Mana Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Mana Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Selfish Caster	DESC:You lack a source of magical empathy. You cannot gain or use [manabond] talents or create manabonds, but you may still be targeted by manabonds created by other creatures. Incompatible: Selfish Caster Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc182
Sphere Drawback - Selfish Caster	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Mana Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Mana Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Incongruent	DESC:Your source of magic is unstable, and interacts poorly with the mana within other spellcasters. You may not use [manipulation] talents, and may not take talents that allow you to grant spell points or talents to other creatures. Incompatible: Incongruent Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc183
Sphere Drawback - Weapon-bound	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Mana Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Mana Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Your Mana sphere talents fizzle without a physical vessel to deliver them. You may only deliver an [expunge] or a [manipulation] through the use of the Manasurge Strike talent. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc184
Sphere Drawback - Addling Brew	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Mind Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Mind Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:You must select the Instill Charm talent with the bonus talent granted by this drawback, and you can only use your Mind sphere abilities through this talent. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc186
Sphere Drawback - Animal Shaman	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Mind Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Mind Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Kindred Knack	DESC:You may affect animals with your Mind sphere effects, but not creatures of your own creature type. You must choose the Recondite Stimuli advanced talent as the bonus talent gained from this drawback, and must choose vermin with that talent. Incompatible: Kindred Knack Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc187
Sphere Drawback - Blatant Side-Effects	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Mind Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Mind Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Your mind-affecting magic acts more like a hammer than a scalpel, and produces odd, unintended changes in your target, effectively giving your mind-affecting effects a signature, recognizable trait. Deadpan speech patterns accompanied by an echo and a change in vocabulary, strange glowing halos, curious tremors in the earth whenever the target draws near, the temporary growth of horns or antlers, or even inexplicably vibrant, sometimes swirling, eyes are just some of the traces that your magical mind-affecting effects might leave on their targets. These side effects vanish without a trace when a target is no longer under the effect of one of your mind-affecting effects, making it incredibly obvious when you are influencing someone’s mind and when you are not. Whatever the nature of the signs, a person speaking to or observing a target so affected will recognize the creature’s signs with a DC 10 Perception check, and may know [either through personal history or a DC 10 Spellcraft check] that the target is under mental control. In addition, a DC 15 Sense Motive check will suggest mental coercion and allow someone to detect the enchantment at work, as will a DC 5 Sense Motive check for incredibly blatant mind-affecting effects [such as the Enthrall or Mind Control talents or the dominate person spell]. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc188
Sphere Drawback - Empath	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Mind Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Mind Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:You do not gain the Suggestion charm. You must select a [charm] talent with the bonus talent granted by this drawback. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc189
Sphere Drawback - Hypnotic Gaze	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Mind Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Mind Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Addling Brew	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Inward Focus	DESC:To affect a target with your charms, you must look them in the eyes. A target must be able to see your eyes [or another part of your body at GM discretion] to be targeted with your charm. A creature may declare they are averting their gaze from your eyes as an immediate action or a free action which can be taken once per round, in which case you gain concealment against them for 1 round but they receive a +4 bonus on any saving throws against your charm for the duration. A creature who shuts their eyes completely [a free action which can be taken once per round, in which case the creature cannot open its eyes until the start of its next turn] or otherwise cannot see you at all cannot be targeted by your charm at all. Your charm effects are considered gaze attacks for any ability that would affect gaze attacks. In order to target yourself with a charm, you must be able to clearly see your reflection in some nearby reflective surface such as a mirror or a pool of water. Whenever you target yourself with a charm sphere effect by looking into a reflection of yourself, you are flat-footed until the beginning of your next turn. You may not use your charms on yourself while you cannot see. You must select a [charm] talent or a talent which affects your charms using this drawback. Incompatible: Addling Brew, Inward Focus Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc190
Sphere Drawback - Inward Focus	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Mind Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Mind Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Source: Spheres Apocrypha: Cognition Talents You cannot use charm effects. You may only select [cognition] talents and talents that augment them, and must select a [cognition] talent with the bonus talent gained from this drawback. Incompatible: Any Mind drawback that retains or affects a [charm] talent. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc191
Sphere Drawback - Kindred Knack	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Mind Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Mind Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Animal Shaman	DESC:You may not affect creatures of your own creature type, and the Expanded Charm talent does not allow you to affect creatures of your own creature type. The bonus magic talent gained from this drawback must be the Recondite Stimuli advanced talent. Incompatible: Animal Shaman Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc192
Sphere Drawback - Lost In Translation	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Mind Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Mind Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Your charms become language dependent effects; the targets of your [charm] talents must share a language with you in order for the charms to take effect, and the language must be properly spoken to them as part of the casting. Creatures incapable of hearing you cannot be affected by your charms. You may not select or use [cloud] talents. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc193
Sphere Drawback - Tactile Charm	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Mind Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Mind Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:The range of your Mind sphere effects such as charms and clouds decreases from close to touch. Using a charm on a target requires you to touch them first, which usually requires a melee touch attack as part of using the charm. You must select the Charming Strike talent as the bonus talent from this drawback, and can only use that talent when making melee attacks. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc194
Sphere Drawback - Unusual Entreatment	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Mind Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Mind Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Animal Shaman	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Kindred Knack	DESC:Source: Expanded Spheres: Baron's Lost Apocrypha Choose a creature type other than your own. You may affect creatures of that type with your Mind sphere effects, but not creatures of your own type. You do not gain a bonus talent from this drawback. Incompatible: Animal Shaman, Kindred Knack Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc195
Sphere Drawback - Holistic Brew	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Nature Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Nature Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:You must select the Instill Spirit talent with the bonus talent granted by this drawback, and you can only use your Nature sphere abilities through this talent. You must possess the Limited Nature talent twice to gain this drawback. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc197
Sphere Drawback - Limited Nature	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Nature Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Nature Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:You gain only a single geomancing ability of your starting Nature package. For example, if you have the [plant] package, you gain only Entangle, Harvest, or Pummel. You must take a [geomancing] talent with the bonus talent gained from this drawback. You may take this drawback twice. If taken twice, you cannot use geomancing powers at all, only [spirit] talents. Instead of a [geomancing] talent, you gain the Master Of Elements talent and one [spirit] talent of your choice as the bonus talents gained from this drawback. Wiki Note: This means you don't have a base geomancing package. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc198
Sphere Drawback - Alternate Aegis	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Protection Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Protection Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Limited Protection	DESC:You do not gain the Deflection aegis. You must use the talent gained with this drawback to acquire an [aegis] talent. Incompatible: Limited Protection [ward] Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc200
Sphere Drawback - Aligned Protection	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Protection Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Protection Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Choose an end of the alignment spectrum that you possess [good, evil, lawful, or chaotic]. Your aegises and wards only provide protection against creatures of the opposite alignment [evil for good, lawful for chaotic, etc.]. Creatures who possess your selected alignment or are neutral [those who possess neither your selected alignment nor its opposite] are not stopped by your barriers, hindered by your wards, and your aegises provide no protection against effects that originate from those creatures. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc201
Sphere Drawback - Circle Of Symbols	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Protection Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Protection Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Limited Protection	DESC:Your wards consist of circles of glowing symbols and runes with no true physicality. You cannot use the barrier ward and cannot take talents that augment barriers, such as Greater Barrier, Buttressing, Barrier Maze, or other, similar talents. You must use the bonus talent gained from this drawback to select a [ward] talent. Incompatible: Limited Protection [aegis] Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc202
Sphere Drawback - Crystalline	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Protection Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Protection Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Limited Protection	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Luminous	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Second Skin	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Shielding	DESC:Your aegis abilities create a physical lattice of crystal around the creature bearing the aegis. It can not be removed without destroying it, and any part that is broken off disappears. A Spellcraft check against a DC equal to 15 + 1/2 your caster level can identify what the lattice is. This requires some means of perceiving magic [such as the Divination sphere’s divine ability]. The lattice can be sundered as if it were a piece of armor. It has a hardness equal to 5 + 1 for every 4 caster levels, and hit points equal to 4 + your caster level. In addition, it provides no defense from touch attacks by incorporeal creatures or light-based attacks. You must use the talent gained with this drawback to acquire an [aegis] talent. Incompatible: Limited Protection [ward], Luminous, Second Skin, Shielding Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc203
Sphere Drawback - Limited Protection	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Protection Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Protection Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Choose either aegis or ward. You lose the other ability and cannot take talents that only grant or alter the lost ability. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc204
Sphere Drawback - Luminous	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Protection Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Protection Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Crystalline	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Limited Protection	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Second Skin	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Shielding	DESC:Your Protection sphere abilities take on the form of an aura or field of light. The light is not powerful enough to be used as a light source, but makes the presence of the protection ability obvious to anyone within 30 feet. Creatures wearing an aegis you created can not benefit from stealth, invisibility, or concealment. Effects that dispel light [such as Dark effects] dispel your Protection sphere abilities as well. You must use the bonus talent gained from this drawback to gain an [aegis] talent. Incompatible: Crystalline, Limited Protection [ward], Second Skin, Shielding Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc205
Sphere Drawback - Protected Soul	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Protection Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Protection Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Limited Protection	DESC:You cannot target other creatures with your aegis, only yourself. You must use the bonus talent gained from this drawback to gain an [aegis] talent. Incompatible: Limited Protection [ward] Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc206
Sphere Drawback - Protective Brew	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Protection Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Protection Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Limited Protection	DESC:You must select the Instill Aegis talent with the bonus talent granted by this drawback, and you can only use your aegises through this talent. Incompatible: Limited Protection [ward] Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc207
Sphere Drawback - Second Skin	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Protection Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Protection Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Crystalline	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Luminous	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Limited Protection	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Shielding	DESC:Your aegis not only surrounds creatures, it enchants their skin directly. You may only apply an aegis to a creature who is wearing no armor, and wearing armor suppresses its effects. You must use the bonus talent gained from this drawback to gain an [aegis] talent. Incompatible: Crystalline, Luminous, Limited Protection [ward], Shielding Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc208
Sphere Drawback - Shielding	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Protection Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Protection Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Crystalline	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Luminous	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Second Skin	DESC:Your aegis takes the form of an energy shield that you use to intercept attacks. You can not create any aegis that protects a creature from the environment [such as Breathless], and creatures lose the benefit of your aegis against attacks that would bypass a shield or when they are flat-footed. You must use the bonus talent gained from this drawback to take the Shared Aegis talent. Incompatible: Crystalline, Luminous, Second Skin Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc209
Sphere Drawback - Machine Gremlin	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Technomancy Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Technomancy Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Your sprites cannot be used to enhance machinery. You cannot use the Boost program with your sprites. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc211
Sphere Drawback - Outmoded Encroachment	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Technomancy Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Technomancy Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:The hazardous effects of your sprites are stopped by commonplace countermeasures. You cannot use the Drain and Interfere programs with your sprites. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc212
Sphere Drawback - Relic Wielder	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Technomancy Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Technomancy Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Your ability to interfere with magical equipment does not extend to technological devices. You cannot use your Technomancy sphere abilities to affect technological items. You must select the Relic Manipulation advanced talent with this drawback. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc213
Sphere Drawback - Volatile Sprites	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Technomancy Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Technomancy Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Your sprites cause machines to act erratically. You gain Glitch-Prone Sprites as a bonus talent, but all of your sprite hosts are always considered timeworn for the purpose of triggering glitches. This drawback does not grant any additional bonus talents. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc214
Sphere Drawback - Directional Control	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Telekinesis Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Telekinesis Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Flight	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Gravity	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Orbit	DESC:Choose either directly towards you or directly away from you. When you affect targets with telekinesis, you can only move them in the selected direction. You cannot affect yourself and you cannot perform actions such as lifting targets or creating sustained forces unless the movement is entirely in the selected direction. You must choose Acceleration as the talent gained from this drawback. Incompatible: Flight, Gravity, Orbit Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc216
Sphere Drawback - Flight	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Telekinesis Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Telekinesis Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Directional Control	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Gravity	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Limited Telekinesis	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Orbit	DESC:You can only use telekinesis to lift creatures. You must select the Flight talent with the bonus talent gained from this drawback, and cannot use telekinesis unless it also uses that talent. Incompatible: Directional Control, Gravity, Limited Telekinesis, Orbit Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc217
Sphere Drawback - Gravity	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Telekinesis Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Telekinesis Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Directional Control	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Limited Telekinesis	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Flight	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Orbit	DESC:You have power over gravity. You can only gain Telekinesis talents that affect gravity such as Gravity Shift, Gravity Ward, or Gravity Well, and must choose one such talent as the bonus talent gained from this drawback. You cannot use telekinesis except through one of those talents. Incompatible: Directional Control, Limited Telekinesis, Flight, Orbit Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc218
Sphere Drawback - Limited Telekinesis	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Telekinesis Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Telekinesis Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Flight	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Gravity	DESC:You may only use your telekinesis on one type of material [water, metal, stone, etc.] chosen when you gain this drawback. If you are an armorist, you may select weapons or equipment you have made with your bound equipment and summon equipment class features as your ‘material type’. If you possess the Blood sphere and have selected ‘blood’ as your material, you may use your telekinesis abilities on creatures under the effects of your blood control. Incompatible: Flight, Gravity Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc219
Sphere Drawback - Orbit	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Telekinesis Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Telekinesis Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Directional Control	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Flight	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Gravity	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Passive Telekinesis	DESC:You must choose Orbit as the bonus talent gained from this drawback. You may only use telekinesis to place objects in, remove them from, or use objects contained within your orbit. Incompatible: Directional Control, Flight, Gravity, Passive Telekinesis Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc220
Sphere Drawback - Passive Telekinesis	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Telekinesis Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Telekinesis Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Flight	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Gravity	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Orbit	DESC:You possess the ability to maneuver your telekinesis in delicate ways, but find direct force difficult. You cannot use your telekinesis to perform a Bludgeon attack. You must select Telekinetic Tools as the bonus talent gained from this drawback. Incompatible: Flight, Gravity, Orbit Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc221
Sphere Drawback - Altered Time	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Time Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Time Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Choose either Haste or Slow. You lose this ability. You may take this drawback twice, losing both Haste and Slow. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc223
Sphere Drawback - Personal Time	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Time Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Time Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Temporal Blade	DESC:You may only affect yourself when using alter time abilities that affect creatures. You cannot gain the Ranged Time or Mass Time talents. You must select a [time] talent or Improved Haste with the bonus talent gained from this drawback. Incompatible: Temporal Blade Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc224
Sphere Drawback - Temporal Blade	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Time Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Time Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Personal Time	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Temporal Brew	DESC:You must select the Time Strike talent with the bonus talent gained from this drawback. You cannot use any alter time ability except through the use of the Time Strike talent. Incompatible: Personal Time, Temporal Brew Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc225
Sphere Drawback - Temporal Brew	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Time Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Time Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Temporal Blade	DESC:You must select the Instill Time talent with the bonus talent granted by this drawback, and you can only use your Time sphere abilities through this talent. Incompatible: Temporal Blade Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc226
Sphere Drawback - Alternate Rally	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,War Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom War Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Commando	DESC:You cannot use the Commanding Aid rally. You must choose a [rally] talent with the bonus talent gained from this drawback. Incompatible: Commando Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc228
Sphere Drawback - Alternate Totem	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,War Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom War Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Battle Manipulation	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Small Unit Strategist	DESC:You cannot use Totem Of War. You must choose a [totem] talent with the bonus talent gained from this drawback. Incompatible: Battle Manipulation, Small Unit Strategist Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc229
Sphere Drawback - Battle Manipulation	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,War Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom War Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Alternate Totem	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Personal Conflict	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Small Unit Strategist	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Squadron Elite	DESC:You cannot create totems. You must select Eternal Vigilance with the bonus talent gained through this drawback, unless you also possess Solo Combatant, in which case any War talent you qualify for can be selected. Incompatible: Alternate Totem, Personal Conflict, Small Unit Strategist, Squadron Elite Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc230
Sphere Drawback - Commando	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,War Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom War Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Alternate Rally	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Battle Manipulation	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Solo Combatant	DESC:You cannot use rallies. You must select a [mandate] talent or a [momentum] talent with the bonus talent gained through this drawback. Incompatible: Alternate Rally, Battle Manipulation, Solo Combatant Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc231
Sphere Drawback - Exploitable Momentum	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,War Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom War Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Source: Baron’s Uncanny Gateway Your strategies leave you open to a clever opponent. As long as you have momentum, once per round an enemy within range of your [momentum] talents may spend one point of momentum for your pool to fuel one of their own [momentum] abilities or to gain a +4 morale bonus to a single attack roll as a swift action. You must select either Combat Inertia or Resourcefulness as the bonus talent from this drawback. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc232
Sphere Drawback - Manifest Totem	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,War Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom War Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Battle Manipulation	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Personal Conflict	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Small Unit Strategist	DESC:Your totems manifest as Medium-sized physical objects that cannot be moved [except by effects that could normally move a totem]. The object has a number of hit points equal to your caster level, AC equal to 10 + 1/2 your caster level, and saving throw bonuses equal to 2 + 1/2 your caster level. The object is transparent enough to not block line of sight but may be used to provide cover. Destruction of the object ends the totem’s effects. You must select a [totem] talent as the talent gained from this drawback. You cannot select the Totemic Aura or Totemic Emblem talent so long as you possess this drawback, nor can you attach your totems to other targets or effects [such as through the Tribal Rhythm feat]. Incompatible: Battle Manipulation, Personal Conflict, Small Unit Strategist Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc233
Sphere Drawback - Personal Conflict	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,War Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom War Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Battle Manipulation	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Small Unit Strategist	DESC:You can only create totems attached to creatures. You must choose Totemic Aura as the bonus talent gained from this drawback. Turning any totem you create into a fixed totem [such as through the use of the Redeployment talent] dispels it. You can create mandates and rallies normally. You may take this drawback twice. If taken twice, you may only attach totemic auras to yourself. If taken twice, you must choose Call To Arms with the bonus talent gained from this drawback. Incompatible: Battle Manipulation, Small Unit Strategist Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc234
Sphere Drawback - Small Unit Strategist	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,War Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom War Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Alternate Totem	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Battle Manipulation	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Personal Conflict	DESC:You cannot create totems. You must select a [mandate] talent or a [momentum] talent with the bonus talent gained through this drawback. Incompatible: Alternate Totem, Battle Manipulation, Personal Conflict Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc235
Sphere Drawback - Solo Combatant	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,War Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom War Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Commando	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Squadron Elite	DESC:You cannot target other creatures with your rallies, only yourself. You must select Eternal Vigilance with the bonus talent gained through this drawback, unless you also possess Battle Manipulation, in which case any War talent you qualify for can be selected. Incompatible: Commando, Squadron Elite Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc236
Sphere Drawback - Squadron Elite	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,War Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom War Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Battle Manipulation	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Solo Combatant	DESC:Your War magic only works for those in your squadron. Creatures outside your squadron cannot be affected by your totems, be rallied, use momentum, or be in mandates. When you take this drawback, you do not gain a bonus talent. Instead, you gain the Squadron Commander feat. Incompatible: Battle Manipulation, Solo Combatant Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc237
Sphere Drawback - Bender	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Warp Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Warp Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Inanimate Teleport	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Personal Warp	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Short Teleport	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Splintering Teleport	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Taxing Teleport	DESC:You cannot teleport, you may only bend space. You must select a [space] talent with the bonus talent gained through this drawback. Incompatible: Inanimate Teleport, Personal Warp, Short Teleport, Splintering Teleport, Taxing Teleport Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc239
Sphere Drawback - Distorting Presence	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Warp Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Warp Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:Your [space] talents are tied to your location, twisting your immediate environment. You gain Distortion Aura as the bonus talent for this drawback, but must use it in conjunction with any [space] talent that you create [preventing you from using the talent’s normal range]. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc240
Sphere Drawback - Exploit Fragility	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Warp Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Warp Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Bender	DESC:Source: Baron’s Uncanny Gateway Your abilities rely on a certain “thinness” between dimensions to function. You may only use your teleport to enter or leave areas that are already affected by a [space] talent or other interplanar effect at GM discretion. You cannot select a [space] talent with this drawback. Incompatible: Bender Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc241
Sphere Drawback - Inanimate Teleport	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Warp Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Warp Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Bender	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Personal Warp	DESC:You cannot teleport creatures, only objects. You must select Teleport Object with the bonus talent you gain from this drawback. Incompatible: Bender, Personal Warp Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc242
Sphere Drawback - Limited Warp	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Warp Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Warp Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:You may only teleport or bend space when within an area that meets a specific condition and can only choose a destination for teleport that also matches that condition. Choose one of the following conditions or speak with your GM about finding another appropriate one: you can only teleport or bend space in areas of dim light or darkness; you can only teleport or bend space in a body of water; you can only teleport or bend space when touching fire; you can only teleport or bend space when touching a living tree. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc243
Sphere Drawback - Personal Warp	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Warp Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Warp Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Bender	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Inanimate Teleport	DESC:You may only target yourself with your teleport ability. You cannot gain talents that specifically target others such as Mass Teleport, Swap Placement, or Unwilling Teleport, and cannot gain a [space] talent as the talent gained from this drawback. Incompatible: Bender, Inanimate Teleport Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc244
Sphere Drawback - Short Teleport	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Warp Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Warp Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Bender	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Taxing Teleport	DESC:The range of your teleport is limited to 10 feet plus an additional 5 feet per 4 caster levels. You may not spend a spell point to increase your teleport range. If another talent would alter the range of your teleport, use the shorter of the two ranges. You cannot take Distant Teleport. You must select Emergency Teleport, Quick Teleport or Swap Placement as the bonus talent from this drawback. Incompatible: Bender, Taxing Teleport Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc245
Sphere Drawback - Splintering Teleport	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Warp Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Warp Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Bender	DESC:Whether due to the style of your teleportation, incomplete training, or some other phenomenon, whenever you teleport a subject they suffer damage in transit. You must select Splinter with the bonus talent you gain from this drawback and must always apply its effects to your teleport. Incompatible: Bender Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc246
Sphere Drawback - Taxing Teleport	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Warp Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Warp Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Bender	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Short Teleport	DESC:When you teleport, you must always pay a spell point to increase your teleport range, even if you are teleporting a shorter distance. You must select Distant Teleport as the bonus talent from this drawback. Incompatible: Bender, Short Teleport Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc247
Sphere Drawback - Warping Brew	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Warp Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Warp Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:You must select the Instill Teleport talent with the bonus talent granted by this drawback, and you can only use your Warp sphere abilities through this talent. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc248
Sphere Drawback - Atmospheric Brew	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Weather Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Weather Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Limited Weather	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Small Weather	DESC:You must select the Instill Weather talent with the bonus talent granted by this drawback, and you can only use your Weather sphere abilities through this talent. You must possess the Localized Weather drawback to select this one. Incompatible: Limited Weather, Small Weather Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc250
Sphere Drawback - Limited Weather	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Weather Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Weather Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Atmospheric Brew	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Localized Weather	DESC:You may only affect one weather category: Aridity, Ash, Cold, Heat, Precipitation, Vog, or Wind. If you choose Aridity you may lower the severity of Precipitation but cannot increase it. If you choose Cold you may lower the severity of Heat but cannot increase it. If you choose Heat you may lower the severity of Cold but cannot increase it. If you choose Precipitation you may lower the severity of Aridity but cannot increase it. You cannot take talents that alter an aspect of weather you cannot affect. If the chosen category requires an additional talent to be used, you must select the appropriate talent as the bonus talent, otherwise you must select Severe Weather with the talent gained from this drawback. Incompatible: Atmospheric Brew, Localized Weather. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc251
Sphere Drawback - Localized Weather	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Weather Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Weather Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Limited Weather	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Small Weather	DESC:You do not gain the ability to control weather and you cannot take talents that improve this ability. You must select a [shroud] or [mantle] talent with the bonus talent gained from this drawback. Incompatible: Limited Weather, Small Weather Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc252
Sphere Drawback - Personal Mantle	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Weather Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Weather Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	DESC:You cannot place your mantle on other creatures. When you take this drawback, you do not gain an additional talent. Instead, you gain the Mantled Caster feat, even if you do not meet its prerequisites. Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc253
Sphere Drawback - Small Weather	CATEGORY:Custom Sphere Drawback	COST:0	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Magic Talent,Weather Sphere	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Weather Drawback Talent|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_SPHERE_DRAWBACKS|1	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Atmospheric Brew	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Sphere Drawback,Sphere Drawback - Localized Weather	DESC:The size of your weather is very limited; the maximum size area you can control weather has a close range-sized radius. You must select Focused Weather with the talent gained from this drawback. Incompatible: Atmospheric Brew, Localized Weather Removing it costs a magic talent from that sphere.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/casting-traditions#toc254
